{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we first need to determine the \\(x\\)- and \\(y\\)-intercepts of the function \\(f(x) = \\frac{(x-2)^2 - 9}{3}\\).\n\n### Step 1: Find the \\(y\\)-intercept\nThe \\(y\\)-intercept occurs when \\(x = 0\\). Substituting \\(x = 0\\) into the function, we get:\n\\[\nf(0) = \\frac{(0-2)^2 - 9}{3} = \\frac{4 - 9}{3} = \\frac{-5}{3} = -\\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\nSo, the \\(y\\)-intercept is \\(\\left(0, -\\frac{5}{3}\\right)\\).\n\n### Step 2: Find the \\(x\\)-intercepts\nThe \\(x\\)-intercepts occur when \\(f(x) = 0\\). Setting \\(f(x) = 0\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x-2)^2 - 9}{3} = 0 \\implies (x-2)^2 - 9 = 0 \\implies (x-2)^2 = 9 \\implies x-2 = \\pm 3 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = -1\n\\]\nSo, the \\(x\\)-intercepts are \\((5, 0)\\) and \\((-1, 0)\\).\n\n","prefix_end":713,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1156,1184,311,8253,279,17767,87,59,7287,323,17767,88,59,7287,2245,57771,315,279,729,17767,69,2075,8,284,1124,37018,96065,87,12,17,29776,17,481,220,24,15170,18,11035,3593,14374,14822,220,16,25,7379,279,17767,88,59,7287,2245,1484,198,785,17767,88,59,7287,2245,1484,13666,979,17767,87,284,220,15,59,568,3719,3696,10607,17767,87,284,220,15,57758,1119,279,729,11,582,633,510,59,9640,69,7,15,8,284,1124,37018,96065,15,12,17,29776,17,481,220,24,15170,18,92,284,1124,37018,90,19,481,220,24,15170,18,92,284,1124,37018,19999,20,15170,18,92,284,481,59,37018,90,20,15170,18,532,59,921,4416,11,279,17767,88,59,7287,2245,1484,374,1124,11520,2359,7,15,11,481,59,37018,90,20,15170,18,11035,1291,10699,3593,14374,14822,220,17,25,7379,279,17767,87,59,7287,2245,57771,198,785,17767,87,59,7287,2245,57771,12170,979,17767,69,2075,8,284,220,15,59,568,20037,17767,69,2075,8,284,220,15,59,701,582,614,510,59,9640,59,37018,96065,87,12,17,29776,17,481,220,24,15170,18,92,284,220,15,1124,6383,550,320,87,12,17